# Logging & Configuration

## Logging with Logrus

When using logrus, import with the `log` alias:
```go
log "github.com/sirupsen/logrus"
```

Note: Some files use stdlib `log` instead of logrus (e.g., `authenticator.go`, `store.go`). Don't assume all `log.` calls are logrus.

Use appropriate levels:
- `log.Debug("List Publications")` — verbose tracing
- `log.Println("Server starting on port " + port)` — informational
- `log.Warningf("Registration halted: device %s already registered", device.ID)` — warnings
- `log.Errorf("error binding request: %v", err)` — errors (use `%v` for error values)
- `log.Fatalf("ListenAndServe error: %v", err)` — fatal, exits the process

Don't use `log.Info()` or `log.Infof()` — this project uses `log.Println()` for info level.

## Configuration

Config is loaded from YAML + environment variables (`envconfig` with `LCPSERVER_` prefix):

```go
cf := &conf.Config{}
envconfig.Process("lcpserver", cf)
```

Sensitive values come from Docker secrets files:
- `LCPSERVER_ACCESS_FILE` — Basic auth credentials
- `MYSQL_PASSWORD_FILE` — DB password
- `JWT_SECRETKEY_FILE` — JWT signing key

## Environment Variables

- `LCPSERVER_CONFIG` — path to YAML config file
- `LCPSERVER_PORT` — server port (default: 8989)
- `LCPSERVER_DSN` — database connection string
- `LCPSERVER_LOGLEVEL` — log level (debug/info/warn/error)
- `LCPSERVER_PUBLICBASEURL` — public-facing base URL
- `LCPENCRYPT_*` — encryption tool config
